- `leashed_leashSubject` PARAMS: {"intent":"Who you collar, who holds it (you / another / None / tied), how, and why. Example — put a rope leash on Tom's neck and hold it myself."} — You put a new collar and leash on someone nearby. Hold it, leave it hanging, or tie them to a point. Not when you are the one getting collared, and not for changing or removing an existing leash.
- `Combat` — Category: a real fight with weapons or magic: attack someone this very moment, or end a fight the speaker is in by surrendering or calling a truce; and its wounds: binding a bleeding wound or splinting a broken bone with one's own hands, no magic. Carrying on a fight already under way needs no action. Threats of what will happen, warnings, readying a weapon, 'prepare to fight' and 'if you…' are words; drawing steel and striking now is the attack. Fist-fights are Brawl; an outlaw questioning the player at their camp is CampChallenge; an ambush standoff is AmbushStandoff; resisting a guard who has stopped one over a bounty is Arrest.
- `leashed_leashLeashed` PARAMS: {"intent":"Who puts the collar on you, who holds it (or None), how, and why. Example — Bob puts a rope leash on my neck and holds it."} — Someone else (including the player) puts a new collar and leash on you. Use when narration already said you were leashed. Dialogue may object; still pick this so the game applies it. Not when you collar someone else, and not for changing or removing an existing leash.
**Guidelines:**
- Only use an action if it matches what you said, agreed to, or are doing
- Agreement can be implicit—positive responses or steps toward fulfilling a request count
- You can initiate actions unprompted if it fits your character
- Some entries are **action categories** that group related actions (e.g., "Inventory", "Economy"). Selecting a category triggers a follow-up to pick the specific action within it
- **REQUIRED**: When selecting a category, you MUST include `PARAMS: {"intent": "..."}` describing what you intend to do. Example: `ACTION: Economy PARAMS: {"intent": "sell a health potion to the player for 450 gold"}`. Category selections without intent will fail.
- `TriggerDialogueLine` runs a complete exchange on its own, gold and all (renting a room, training, a quest reward). When one of its codes fits, use it ALONE: never also add `Economy` or another action for the same deal, or the player is charged or rewarded twice
- Output dialogue lines BEFORE the ACTION line (this allows speech to start while action is parsed)
